 "short_name": "Ulundi",
 "_doc": "ULUNDI LOCAL MUNICIPALITY - 'TAX INVOICE / STATEMENT' ledger statement, account E[number removed] (Stand 113, ULUNDI BA, 'Ulundi ETE' in the master list). Same billing vendor as Ditsobotla / uPhongolo / eDumbe, but a DIFFERENT template: there are NO service sub-headings on their own lines - each charge is one ledger row whose DESCRIPTION carries the service, the quantity and the register readings:\n  30-04-2026  Electricity Basic Charge<40KVA                 331,71    2 543,10          -23 932,92\n  30-04-2026  Electricity Demand Charge 0KVA - [0 to 0]         0,00        0,00          -23 932,92\n  30-04-2026  Electricity Consumption 25846KWH - [103600 to 129446]  12 454,93  95 487,79   71 554,87\nLedger columns are Date / Description / VAT / Debit / Credit / Balance. THE DEBIT COLUMN IS VAT-INCLUSIVE and the VAT is printed separately, so every ex-VAT figure is derived per line with a 'sub' compute (never read the inclusive figure into an ex-VAT column).\nUnder the Demand and Consumption rows sits a meter table:\n  Meter Number  Previous/Current Reading Date  Tariff  Consumption   Exclusive\n  E-[number removed]   31-03-2026  30-04-2026   3,21   25 846,00            83 032,86\n  Kwh\nThe register UNIT (Kwh / Kva) is printed on the line BELOW the data row - that is the only way to tell the two meter rows apart, so both rules end in '\\n Kwh$' / '\\n Kva$'. The table prints reading DATES only, never reading values; the register readings come from the description bracket '[103600 to 129446]'. The 'Exclusive' column is the bill's OWN ex-VAT amount and is used in preference to the derived one (they agree to <=R0.01).\nMONEY IS PRINTED COMMA-DECIMAL / SPACE-THOUSANDS ('95 487,79'). The engine's _to_decimal strips the comma as a thousands separator, which would make every figure 100x too big, so - following the Ditsobotla convention - every money pattern captures the RAND PART ONLY '(-?\\d{0,3}(?:[ ]\\d{3})*),\\d{2}' (each figure therefore reads up to R0.99 LOW) and the exact printed string is kept in a parallel *_txt native field. Quantity columns always end ',00' so kWh/kVA are exact.\nSingle-band industrial supply: one kWh register + one kVA demand register, no TOU. Following the Ekurhuleni/KwaDukuza/Ditsobotla convention the single energy register is routed to the STANDARD band. The bill prints NO reading type, NO NMD, NO TOU bands and NO total-VAT / total-ex-VAT line, so those canonical columns are '_none' and total_ex_vat_r is necessarily the sum of the three parts (Rule Zero: the reconcile check is therefore circular for this municipality - the genuine check is the printed 'Exclusive' column against Debit-VAT, plus VAT/Exclusive = 15%).\nThe bill prints no street address for the site (only Stand Number / Town / Category), so site_name is a concat of the stand number and the town.\n1-page and 2-page renderings of the identical statement both occur (2-page repeats the masthead above the ageing block); 'ULU_113_Statement-30 September 2025_0.pdf' is only 77KB because it is a 1-page rendering - it is a COMPLETE statement, not a nil one, and needs no special handling.\nThe Payment ledger row sits ABOVE the first 'Electricity Basic Charge' row (so it is in the header, not in a section) and a month can carry several ('Payment - Electricity Basic' / '- Electricity Consumption' / '- Electricity Demand Charge'), so the payment rules are 'document' scope with collect:'sum'. Note that summing N rand-truncated figures accumulates the truncation: the payment total can read up to N x R0.99 low.",
